{"comment":"The repository channel on two connections, on the fixture repository ${repo}: a virtual branch synced before, whose session the host opens on the first subscribe from the frame of the fixture (the warm start), so ${view0} is the seed. The first connection is a Tauri shell with the windows main and review-1, the second a bridge with its one mirror window. A subscription is a window's, and each action goes to each subscribed window in a frame of its own. A token ${name} binds at its first appearance in a host line to the value there, and each later appearance is that value; ${name.field} is a field of a bound value; ${any} matches any value. A host line of one connection may come before or after a host line of another: the order holds within a connection. serverSeq is one counter of the host. A step line is an action of the runner on the fixture between the frames. A client line marked invalid breaks the schema on purpose."}
{"client":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"channel":"ahp-root://","protocolVersions":["1.0.0"],"clientId":"corpus-1","clientInfo":{"name":"branch-deck-app","build":"${build}"},"_meta":{"x-branch-deck":{"version":"1.0.0","capabilities":{"folderDialog":true,"updater":true,"restart":true,"agentCli":true,"nativeMenu":true,"hostRequests":["openWindow","showWindow","notify"]}}}}},"conn":1}
{"host":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"1.0.0","serverSeq":0,"snapshots":[],"serverInfo":{"name":"branch-deck","build":"${build}"},"_meta":{"x-branch-deck":{"version":"1.0.0"}}}},"conn":1}
